  "pse": {
    "problem": "Data silos and data privacy issues in federated learning, where multiple participants need to train models together without exchanging sensitive data.",
    "solution_function": "The system performs co-training based on two model tasks (one from the first participant and one from the second participant) to obtain a federated learning model. The first participant's platform associates its pre-created configuration information with the second participant's pre-created configuration information, verifies the first configuration information, sends a creation request to the second participant's platform if verification passes, receives confirmation when the second configuration information is verified, and creates a first model task. The second participant's platform verifies its own configuration information when it receives the creation request, creates a second model task based on its own configuration information if verification passes, and sends a confirmation message to the first participant's platform.",
    "solution_structure": "The system comprises association, verification, sending, and creation modules in the first participant's platform, and a similar setup in the second participant's platform.",
    "solution_implementation": "The system operates by associating configuration information between participants, verifying configuration information, sending creation requests, creating model tasks, and performing co-training based on these tasks.",
    "effect": "The solution allows for data privacy preservation while still enabling multiple participants to train a federated learning model together."
  },
